{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "First Programming Languages", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about the history of programming languages.   ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Give detailed and important information regarding to the history of language programming in different periods of time.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Compound Nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Compound nouns</strong> are words which are made up of <strong>two or more words</strong>. By adding another word, you will have a new word with a different meaning. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Since we didn't get to finish last class, today we're going to continue with the topic: History of programming languages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you think our forebears could forecast how programming would be in the future? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The key features of FORTRAN are currently used in aerospace, automotive industries, government, and research institutions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "COBOL was designed to be user-friendly and it used to be applied by the United States Postal Service. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Compound nouns are generally made by putting together: noun + noun, adjective + noun, verb + noun. </br></br> Remember that a compound noun can be a single word, as two words, or words with a hyphen.</br></br> <strong>Closed or solid compound words:</strong> These words can be a <strong>single</strong> word. </br> </br>   <ul> <li>keyboard</li> \t<li>anyone</li> \t<li>something</li> \t<li>aerospace</li> \t<li>software</li> </ul>  <strong>Space or open compound words:</strong> They are word with a  <strong>space</strong> in between.</br> </br>  <ul> <li>home page</li> \t<li>disk drive</li> \t<li>web site</li> <li>virtual reality</li> <li>search engine</li> </ul> <strong>Hyphenated words:</strong> These words have a hyphen in between. </br>  </br><ul> <li>one-sided</li> \t<li>follow-up</li> \t<li>check-in</li>  <li>high-tech</li> <li>long-term</li> </ul></br>It is essential to know that most of the words don't keep their initial meaning. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Tense in Negative with Time Expressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Simple past is used when you want to talk about completed actions that took place at a certain point in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The simple past tense in negative is made by using the auxiliary did + not: <strong>did not or didn't.</strong>  When you use the auxiliary <strong>did</strong>, the action verb comes in base form.</br></br>   Take a look at the following structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<div align=\"center\"><strong>Subject + did not or didn't + verb in base form + complement</strong></div>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<i>I <strong>didn't know</strong> anything about programming languages. </i> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The simple past tense in negative with the verb to be is made by using <strong>was + not</strong> and <strong>were + not</strong> or <strong>wasn't and weren't.</strong>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at the following structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<i>Sophie <strong>wasn't</strong> very sharp to find out more about programming languages.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use simple past tense, you can also use<strong> time expressions</strong> to specify the moment actions happened in the past. Such as:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">Yesterday</br><span class=\"bullet\">The day before yesterday</br><span class=\"bullet\">Last year</br> <span class=\"bullet\">Last Morning</ul", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Its history didn't start in the 20th century.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well, I guess they didn't think it could ever be so important for us nowadays. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Then, Basic Language didn't initiate until 1964.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Created as a simplified language, it was designed for those who didn't have a technical background to avoid making intellectual effort.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "forecast ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to predict a future action ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now, Sophie, do you think our forebears could forecast how programming would be in the future?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " forebear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ancestor", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you think our forebears could forecast how programming would be in the future?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content